From: EasyMesh labs
Subject: [PATCH] wmediumd: a tracked clone's EINVAL is transient again

Patch 0011 classified hwsim's EINVAL for a cloned frame this process sent and
tracked as RF delivery loss (the receiving radio idle, scanning or between
channel contexts): logged at debug level, and since 0014 counted as
netlink_clone_einval, as the console's reference still says. Patch 0022
dropped that branch: every such refusal was logged at error level and counted
as netlink_other_errors. On rdk-1004 (9 October) hundreds of them during a room
restart read as medium faults.

Restore the classification for tracked command-2 EINVAL only; untracked
sequences, other errors and refused TX status (command 3, which can also mean
hwsim dropped pending frames because the medium fell behind) stay errors. The
record of clones grows from 4096 to 65536 entries (2 MiB): the lab clones
thousands of frames a second, and a starved medium reads the replies late.

diff --git a/wmediumd/wmediumd.c b/wmediumd/wmediumd.c
index 4458808..60f4b90 100644
--- a/wmediumd/wmediumd.c
+++ b/wmediumd/wmediumd.c
@@ -379,7 +379,10 @@ struct mc_vif_state {
 static struct mc_vif_state *mc_vifs;
 static size_t mc_n_vifs;
 
-#define NL_CLONED_FRAME_TRACK_SLOTS 4096
+/* A clone's record must outlive the wait for its error reply: the lab clones
+ * thousands of frames a second (every beacon to every radio in range), and a
+ * busy or starved medium reads the replies late. 65536 records, 2 MiB. */
+#define NL_CLONED_FRAME_TRACK_SLOTS 65536
 struct nl_cloned_frame_track {
 	u32 sequence;
 	struct station *source;
@@ -1462,7 +1465,20 @@ int nl_err_cb(struct sockaddr_nl *nla, struct nlmsgerr *nlerr, void *arg)
 	u32 seq = nlerr->msg.nlmsg_seq;
 	struct nl_cloned_frame_track *track = nl_tracked_cloned_frame(seq);
 
-
+	/* mac80211_hwsim returns EINVAL when a well-formed cloned frame reaches a
+	 * radio while it is idle, stopped, or between channel contexts: normal RF
+	 * delivery loss while a radio scans or changes channel, not a daemon or
+	 * protocol failure (0011). Only requests this process constructed and
+	 * tracked are classified so; malformed or unrelated failures, and refused
+	 * TX status (command 3), remain errors. */
+	if (gnlh->cmd == HWSIM_CMD_FRAME && nlerr->error == -EINVAL && track) {
+		wmd_telemetry_netlink_rejection(ctx, track->source,
+			track->destination, track->frequency_mhz,
+			nlerr->error, true);
+		w_logf(ctx, LOG_DEBUG,
+			"nl: cloned frame not received, seq %u\n", seq);
+		return NL_SKIP;
+	}
 	wmd_telemetry_netlink_rejection(ctx,
 		track ? track->source : NULL,
 		track ? track->destination : NULL,
